        &lt;description&gt;Window server CI record is being updated by two sources - one is loaded from a file once a day at 8:00am with data collected by the end of the previous day, and by the other one - ServiceNow. Let’s imagine that ServiceNow is a discovery tool that performs real-time network scans and gathers detailed system information.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Create a discovery source named "File Load". Hint: a discovery source is a choice on a discovery_source field of the cmdb_ci table.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Create two reconciliation rules for the Windows Server class.&amp;#13;
First: the two discovery sources would have to update Asset Tag and Serial number, but ServiceNow discovery will take precedence.&amp;#13;
Second: the Operating System attribute can also be updated by both discovery sources, but this time File Load must be a ‘primary’ source.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
KB:&amp;#13;
